  message: "Fixed in PR #1724 (dev ecf80859e5), all seven filed shapes plus self.m(...). (1) untyped variable receiver -> ruby:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved with call_construct=method (js WI-nasuf / python / java / go parity). (2-4) bare identifiers -- also a call's receiver and a [] object -- told from local reads by Ruby's lexical rule (_is_ruby_local: parameter, block parameter, rescue/for variable or earlier assignment in the scope; a block's bindings visible only inside it), replacing the parameters-only guard and its now-unused helper; a non-local unresolved name gets WI-napaf's external placeholder. (5) AMB-METHOD (3+ classes define the name): the enclosing class's own method binds, else an unresolved edge with enclosing_class and the owner as module (never 'external', WI-napaf's rule: the name is the project's). (6) super / super(...): unresolved edge for the enclosing method's name with enclosing_class = the declared superclass (module = superclass), which the inherited-calls linker walks. (7) direct recursion: the self edge, as python and java emit it (checked live: both do). (8) self.helper(...): binds the enclosing class's method. LIVE on the filed mastodon instance (analyze_ruby over ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/mastodon on dev ecf80859e5, 31 s): lib/rails/engine_extensions.rb:8 load(ext) -> ruby:EngineExtensions:0-0:load:unresolved, enclosing_class EngineExtensions, call_construct method (before: no edge at all); on the same line the implicit-self 'paths' is recorded and the block parameter 'ext' is not. Production-path tests: test_ruby_silent_call_shapes.py (every shape incl. locals controls, for-variables, top-level super, and K#go -> Base#go through the full pipeline/linker). Two existing tests changed by intent: test_ruby.py obj.process now asserts no RESOLVED bind (the placeholder is new), test_ruby_receiverless_unresolved still passes unchanged because project-name placeholders carry the owner module. NOT MEASURED: corpus frequency per shape (the item left it unmeasured; implicit-self sends will add many external placeholders on Rails apps, which is the intended record). Note: the enclosing class above is the short 'EngineExtensions', not 'Rails::EngineExtensions' -- INV-dosoz."  # b5a0
